      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-296422",
      ":question/problem": "Two local running clubs, club $A$ and club $B$, tracked the distances, in kilometers, run by their members during a weekly fitness challenge. The tables below summarize the number of runners who completed each distance, where club $A$'s results are shown on the left, and club $B$'s on the right.\n\n| DistanceRunners$3$$2$$5$$3$$9$$2$$11$$3$ |  | DistanceRunners$4$$2$$6$$4$$10$$1$$12$$1$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n\nUse the tables to compare the mean distance run by members of each club.\n\nThe mean distance run by members of club $A$ is {{field-1}} $km$.\n\nThe mean distance run by members of club $B$ is {{field-2}} $km$.\n\nThe mean distance run by club $A$'s members is\n{{field-3}}\nthan that of club $B$.\n\n> A calculator is required to answer this question."
