      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-297780",
      ":question/problem": "| Books | Number of Students |\n| --- | ---: |\n| $1$ | $2$ |\n| $3$ | $6$ |\n| $6$ | $2$ |\n| $8$ | $2$ |\n\nTwo groups of students reported the number of books they read last month. The table above summarizes the responses for Group A.\nFor the students in Group B, their average number of books read was $3.6$.\n\nSelect the correct options in the reasoning below.\n\nThe mean number of books read by students in Group A is\n{{field-1}}.\n\nThe mean for Group B is\n{{field-2}}\nthe mean for Group A.\n\nA comparison of the means suggests\n{{field-3}}\nread more books on average last month.\n\n> A calculator is required to answer this question."
